msgid "This topic covers basic Roll and pitch and throttle tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:12
#: e0226327979f449eb31f24238f85467f
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:14
#: 414566cf3add485a9697a8394eac78c8
msgid "After your first flight, you may notice that you copter doesn't respond to control inputs the way you want it to or you may have trouble maintaining control of your copter. If you are familiar with PID controllers, check out the :ref:`advanced tuning guide here <tuning>`. If you are an experienced operator, try out :ref:`the autotune feature <autotune>`. This page will cover the basic tuning section of Mission Planner and APM Planner that simplified the complex tuning process into a few simple sliders. This is the best tuning method for new operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:24
#: c6662d96f1764cf1bbf886563fda6f31
msgid "Roll and pitch tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:26
#: 40be7f6e8792497e963d74ca55422b5b
msgid "Tuning is easiest at the field using a :ref:`telemetry radio <common-telemetry-landingpage>`. Perform an initial flight with the following questions in mind:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:29
#: 8164f7881824404289c567aa38cbd90a
msgid "How does the copter respond to roll and pitch? Is the response more sluggish or twitchy than you want?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:31
#: 1c99a4b1c31b4fdc8268d645e7619269
msgid "When the copter is hover, what level is the throttle set at? Does it hover at the middle position of the stick or is it above or below the center position?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:34
#: ccb7a4c63cb24efc8c7782265562df41
msgid "When raising the throttle, what rate does the copter accelerate at? Does it gain altitude more slowly or more quickly than you want?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:37
#: 3d13f1b909c745a3803f0901d76cf2b8
msgid "Connect the telemetry radio ground module to your ground station computer and open either Mission Planner or APM Planner. Select the correct COM port and select Connect. You should see live data on the Flight Data screen. To begin tuning, select Config/Tuning and Basic Tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:43
#: c01c03bea5ab4f18b24ce3c9cf2a3397
msgid "Start with the Roll/Pitch slider at the top of the page. If you observed that your copter was too twitchy in response to roll and pitch controls, move the slider one tick mark to the left, or, if you observed that your copter was too sluggish, move the slider one tick mark to the right. Repeat your flight to determine if the change was beneficial. Repeat the process until you are satisfied with the way your copter responds to roll and pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:58
#: 00da0317f2ce4bec9d7c0c467b3938a3
msgid "Throttle tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:60
#: e38a025f6f9046639a7c971b34f3b417
msgid "The bottom two sliders allows you to tune the throttle control. Adjust the slider marked Throttle Hover until the copter hovers at the throttle stick's middle position. If the copter hovers with the throttle stick above middle position, move the slider to the left by one tick-mark until it hovers at mid-stick, testing as you go. If the copter hovers with the throttle stick below middle position, move the slider to the right by single tick-mark increments until it does. Make sure to test each set of tuning settings as you go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/basic-tuning.rst:69
#: fc1091652e09404daa20c6f2a19f019c
msgid "Move the slider marked Throttle Accel or Climb Sensitivity to the right to have the copter gain altitude more aggressively or to the left to have the copter gain altitude more gently. Test each increment after setting to evaluate the tune."
msgstr ""
